### Reasoning
The requirement states that when the buffer-to-context table is full on hand-off (fileOut or unknownDataOut) or when a returned buffer is not found in the table, the router must emit a warning event and return the buffer with an empty context. The existing test `testContextTableFull` already verifies the table-full case for both fileOut and unknownDataOut paths. The missing piece is verifying that a returned buffer not found in the table emits the `BufferContextNotFound` event and returns with an empty context. We can reuse the existing helper `testBufferReturn` which already tests this scenario, but we should add it as a dedicated test case for SVC-ROUTER-009 to explicitly verify the requirement.

### New Test Method
```cpp tester
#include "Fw/Types/SuccessEnumAc.hpp"

void FprimeRouterTester::testBufferNotFoundInContextTable() {
    REQUIREMENT("SVC-ROUTER-009");
    // A buffer that was never handed off (no saved context) still returns, but
    // its context is empty and a BufferContextNotFound event is emitted.
    U8 data[1];
    Fw::Buffer buffer(data, sizeof(data));
    this->clearHistory();
    this->invoke_to_fileBufferReturnIn(0, buffer);
    ASSERT_from_dataReturnOut_SIZE(1);  // buffer should be returned via dataReturnOut
    ASSERT_EQ(this->fromPortHistory_dataReturnOut->at(0).data.getData(), data);
    ASSERT_EQ(this->fromPortHistory_dataReturnOut->at(0).data.getSize(), sizeof(data));
    ASSERT_EVENTS_BufferContextNotFound_SIZE(1);
    ComCfg::FrameContext defaultCtx;
    ASSERT_EQ(this->fromPortHistory_dataReturnOut->at(0).context.get_vcId(), defaultCtx.get_vcId());
}
```

